<title>CANADA: Canadian foreign reserves rise in October.</title>
<headline>Canadian foreign reserves rise in October.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian foreign reserve holdings rose during October, the Finance Department said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>   RESERVES			  Oct 96     Sept 96</p>
<p>   Total			   20.029 bln  19.493 bln</p>
<p>   U.S. dollars		  16.958 bln  16.438 bln</p>
<p>   Other foreign currencies     507 million     502 million</p>
<p>   Gold				 156 million     156 million</p>
<p>   Special drawing rights     1.167 bln   1.162 bln</p>
<p>   IMF reserves		   1.241 bln   1.235 bln</p>
<p>Note - Figures in U.S. dollars.  </p>
<p>Official government operations increased reserves by US$157 million.</p>
<p>Details of the changes in the month:</p>
<p>    Gain on gold sales		    +6</p>
<p>    Earnings on investments	    +96</p>
<p>    Revaluation effects		   +8</p>
<p>    Foreign currency debt	     +287</p>
<p>    Other transactions		   -18</p>
<p>NOTE - in millions of U.S. dollars  </p>
<p>During October, net sales of Canada bills totalled $287.2 million, increasing the level of outstanding bills to $5.124 billion.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
